## Synthetic reference and procedure

Reference: tools/voices/AN06.wav
SHA-256: 38f2ae669bbda13d21a6ad446fbbd97ac734729a83cd1633a6e0248fe847b35b
Original VoiceDesign seed: 20302605
Original full prompt and source hashes: tools/voices/AN06-provenance.json
Reference transcript:
Mikrofon stummgeschaltet. Mikrofon aktiviert. Ton stummgeschaltet.
Ein Benutzer hat den Channel betreten.
Ein Benutzer hat die Verbindung getrennt.
Verbindung zum Server wiederhergestellt.

All German production phrases are generated as complete sentences through task
tts, family qwen3_tts, using the Base model, the unmodified synthetic reference
and its complete transcript as per-request voice_ref and reference_text fields
in the batch JSON. The fourth reference sentence differs from the
canonical user_join phrase. The reference transcript must describe the actual
reference and must not be replaced with a desired production phrase.

The top-level provenance pronunciation_aliases.de map applies noXa -> Noksa only
to native target text. Canonical transcripts keep noXa; results.text is canonical
and results.renderText records the actual native text. Import matching validates
the current rendered request exactly. The alias does not alter AN06, its full
reference transcript, the original event seeds or authoring.de settings.

provenance.json records per-language providers, request seeds, token/time
limits, reference hash and mastering settings. Each accepted WAV has its own
metrics/hash and recorded review evidence. Trimming, DC removal, endpoint fades
and loudness normalization are applied. No pitch shift or time stretch is used.
Model-conditioned synthesis can vary by runtime or quantization and may omit,
repeat or add speech. Format checks alone do not authenticate content. ASR
review and listening review are distinct; neither should be claimed without
recorded evidence.

## Redistribution boundary

Qwen model weights and audio.cpp are offline authoring dependencies and are
not packaged in noXa. The noXa original synthetic reference and generated fixed
German recordings use the repository's MIT license. This is a project license
choice for the recordings; it is not an assertion that Apache-2.0 automatically
licenses all generated output. English LJ Speech remains public domain. Former
German MLS/D33 attribution describes the retired assets, not these AN06 WAVs.
